00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.620
Immunization is the process
of becoming immune to

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.140
or protected against a disease,

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.153
usually by receiving a vaccine.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.440
Vaccines stimulate your immune system

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.470
to protect you from certain diseases

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.303
so you won't get sick or get an infection.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.820
Normally, the organs and
cells of your immune system

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.200
defend your body from harmful germs

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.513
such as bacteria and viruses.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.790
Immune cells are constantly
circulating through your body.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.480
They monitor certain substances

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:56.080
on the surfaces of cells called antigens.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.310
Healthy cells have different antigens

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.830
than diseased body cells

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.863
or foreign invaders in the body.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.840
Immune cells usually ignore
the antigens on healthy cells.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.970
But when immune cells come
across antigens on germs,

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.140
they destroy the germ.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.950
Afterward, the immune cell
displays the germ's antigen

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.790
on its surface.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.050
This activates other types of immune cells

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.863
to help get rid of the infection.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.060
For example, some activated immune cells

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.830
recognize the antigen
on infected body cells

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.163
and then destroy them.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:36.900
Other activated immune
cells, called plasma cells,

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.130
make molecules called antibodies.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.470
These antibodies travel through your body

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:46.870
and lock on only to germs that
have its specific antigen.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.863
This marks the germ for destruction.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.020
Then, other immune cells attack the germs

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.483
that have these antibodies.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.560
Once the infection is gone,

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.460
some of the immune cells that
were exposed to the antigen

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.563
become memory immune cells.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.660
In the future, if the same type of germ

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.360
infects your body again,

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.130
the memory immune cells
will be ready to destroy it

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.280
so you don't get sick.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.320
This is called natural immunity.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.423
In many cases, it will
last your whole lifetime.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.290
The problem with getting natural immunity

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.230
from having the disease itself

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:27.500
is that some naturally-acquired infections

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.810
can cause serious complications

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.433
or may even be deadly.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.360
For example, polio can result

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.913
in permanent paralysis or death.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.010
Measles can cause swelling of the brain,

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.790
resulting in permanent
brain damage or death,

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.253
especially in children under age five.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:51.480
And whooping cough,
also known as pertussis,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.270
can cause complications such as pneumonia,

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:57.160
slowed or stopped breathing and death,

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.713
especially in babies
under one year of age.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:04.640
While symptoms may not
be severe in all people,

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.500
it's not possible to know
who will be affected enough

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.973
to become very ill or even die.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.630
Vaccines can protect you
from getting these diseases

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.970
and their harmful symptoms.

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:19.410
Vaccines often contain a small amount

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.700
of weakened or killed germs,

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.540
but some contain genetic material

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.850
such as RNA or DNA

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:30.000
that provide instructions
for your body's own cells

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.703
to make the germ's antigen.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.903
Usually, you receive a vaccine as a shot.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.970
Inside your body, the germ
particles in the vaccine

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:43.900
teach your immune cells
to attack these germs.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.080
This process doesn't make you sick

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.700
but it does cause your
body to make memory cells

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.863
and the antibodies for those germs.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.540
As a result, if that germ
infects your body later in life,

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.380
your immune system is ready
to fight the infection

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.963
so that you don't get sick.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.890
The main types of vaccines include

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.793
live attenuated vaccines,

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.683
inactivated vaccines, toxoid vaccines,

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.933
subunit and conjugate vaccines,

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:21.303
mRNA vaccines, and viral vector vaccines.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:28.810
Live attenuated vaccines use
alive but weakened germs.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.010
They're most like a natural infection

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:33.910
and provide a strong disease immunity.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.900
Examples are the measles, mumps, rubella,

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.043
chicken pox and flu nasal spray vaccines.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:46.330
Inactivated vaccines use
inactive or killed germs.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:50.173
You may need several doses
or booster shots over time.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:55.050
Examples are the hepatitis A, flu, polio,

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.593
and rabies vaccines.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:01.580
Toxoid vaccines protect
against harmful substances

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.903
made by germs called toxins.

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:08.643
They use weakened versions
of the toxins called toxoids.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.000
You may need booster shots

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.223
to maintain protection against diseases.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:17.040
Examples are the diptheria
and tetanus parts

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.523
of the DTaP vaccine.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.650
Subunit and conjugate vaccines

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:24.970
use only a specific part of a germ.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.373
They provide strong immunity
to that key part of the germ.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.810
These vaccines may also
require booster shots.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:36.600
Examples are the pertussis
part of the DTaP vaccine

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.543
and the hepatitis B vaccine.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.490
Instead of using germs or toxins,

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:45.460
mRNA vaccines contain
a special type of RNA

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:49.510
called messenger RNA, or mRNA.

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:52.980
mRNA instructs your cells
to make the germ's antigen,

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:55.430
which triggers an immune response.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.410
These vaccines do not carry live virus

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.890
and do not change your DNA.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:03.623
Examples are certain COVID-19 vaccines.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:10.260
Viral vector vaccines may
use either DNA or mRNA

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.300
to provide cells with instructions

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.140
to make a germ's antigen.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.710
The genetic material is wrapped
in a different safe virus

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.650
to take the instructions into your cells.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:24.390
These vaccines do not change your DNA.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:27.133
Examples are certain COVID-19 vaccines.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.060
It's important to know that vaccines

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:34.583
not only protect you but
your community as well.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.760
Many diseases that vaccines prevent

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.630
are spread from person to person.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:44.290
When only a few people in
your community are vaccinated,

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:46.853
the risk of a disease outbreak is high.

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:50.100
But if most people are vaccinated,

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:53.490
it's much less likely
for a disease to spread.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:57.540
This is called community or herd immunity.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.730
Herd immunity is especially important

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:02.620
to protect people who can't be vaccinated.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:05.610
This includes people with
weakened immune systems,

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.513
serious allergies or
other health conditions.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.670
Vaccines protect you, your
family, and your community

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:16.233
from diseases that can be
dangerous or even deadly.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.360
To find out more about vaccines,

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.093
talk to your healthcare provider.

